lesson: 157
title: Planting trees: both ends, one end, no ends, and around a pond
level: primary-3
stars: 2
explain: First find the number of gaps: length ÷ distance. Then look at the ends.
explain: Trees at both ends: gaps + 1. A tree at one end only: as many trees as gaps. No trees at the ends: gaps - 1. Around a closed path, like a pond: as many trees as gaps.
explain: A 30 m path with a tree every 5 m has 6 gaps: 7 trees with both ends, 6 with one end, 5 with no ends; a pond 30 m around also gets 6 trees.
vars: a=name n=3..30 d=2..10
need: n * d + d <= 330
answer: n
exercise: Trees are planted every {d} m along a road {(n-1)*d} m long, with a tree at both ends. How many trees are there?
exercise: Two houses stand {(n+1)*d} m apart. Between them, bushes are planted every {d} m, but there is no bush right next to a house. How many bushes are planted?
exercise: The shore of a pond is {n*d} m long. A tree is planted every {d} m all the way around it. How many trees are there?
exercise: A path {n*d} m long goes from a gate to a wall. A lamp stands every {d} m, with one at the gate but none at the wall. How many lamps are there?
exercise: A round running track is {n*d} m long, with a flag every {d} m. How many flags are on the track?
exercise: A fence runs {(n-1)*d} m from one corner of a garden to another, with a post every {d} m and a post at each corner. How many posts does the fence have?
test: Between two poles {(n+1)*d} m apart, {a} hangs a lantern every {d} m along the wire. No lanterns hang on the poles. How many lanterns does {a.he} hang?
test: {a} walks around a round lake, {n*d} m in all, and every {d} m there is a bench. How many benches are around the lake?
test: A {(n-1)*d}-metre bridge has a lamp every {d} m, counting both ends of the bridge. How many lamps are on the bridge?
test: A log {(n+1)*d} cm long is cut into pieces of {d} cm each. How many cuts are made?
exercise: A pond in Ohio is {n*d} m around. Nesting boxes for ducks are put every {d} m around the shore. How many boxes are there?
exercise: Two trees stand {(n+1)*d} m apart. Flowers are planted every {d} m between them, but none right next to the trees. How many flowers are planted?
exercise: Along a path in Kent {(n-1)*d} m long, a lamp stands every {d} m, including one at each end. How many lamps are there?
exercise: A road {n*d} m long leads from a school to a river in Canada. A tree is planted every {d} m, starting at the school but not at the river. How many trees are planted?
exercise: A circular fence around a playground in Sydney is {n*d} m long, with a post every {d} m. How many posts does it have?
exercise: How many posts stand in a straight fence {(n-1)*d} m long, if they are {d} m apart and the fence starts and ends with a post?
exercise: Between two walls {(n+1)*d} m apart, hooks are put every {d} m, but not on the walls themselves. How many hooks are there?
exercise: A garden path in Ireland, {n*d} m long, has a lamp every {d} m, with a lamp at the start and none at the end. How many lamps are there?
test: Around a circular flower bed in Wellington, {n*d} m round, {a} puts a stone every {d} m. How many stones does {a.he} put down?
test: A ribbon {(n+1)*d} cm long is cut into pieces {d} cm long. How many cuts are needed?
test: Two flagpoles stand {(n+1)*d} m apart in a park in Toronto. Between them a bin is placed every {d} m, with no bin at either flagpole. How many bins are placed?
test: Along a driveway in Texas {(n-1)*d} m long there is a light every {d} m, counting a light at both ends. How many lights are along the driveway?
test: A lake in Scotland is {n*d} m around. Fishing spots are marked every {d} m along the whole shore. How many spots are marked?
test: A jetty {n*d} m long sticks out from a beach in Western Australia. A lamp stands every {d} m, the first at the beach end and none at the far end. How many lamps are on the jetty?
