exam: It is given that trees are planted at intervals of {d} m along a road of {(n-1)*d} m, a tree standing at either end. Determine the number of trees.
exam: Whereas two houses are situated {(n+1)*d} m apart, and bushes are planted between them at intervals of {d} m, no bush being planted at the site of either house, ascertain the number of bushes so planted.
exam: Ascertain the number of trees planted around a circular pond of circumference {n*d} m, the trees being set at equal intervals of {d} m.
exam: Lanterns are suspended at intervals of {d} m along the closed boundary of a circular park whose perimeter measures {n*d} m. State the number of lanterns so suspended.
exercise: The posts round Grandad's old paddock gave up the ghost, so new posts go in every {d} m all the way round the {n*d} m loop. How many new posts are there?
exercise: Two houses stand {(n+1)*d} m apart. The old hedge between them bit the dust, so new bushes go in every {d} m, but none right next to a house. How many bushes are planted?
test: the pet cemetery — sorry, "memorial garden" — has a path {(n-1)*d} m long, a bench every {d} m and one at each end. how many benches, dammit
